===Etymology 2===
{{multiple images|direction=vertical
|image1=Craps.jpg|caption1=A pair of common dice with six sides each.
|image2=Dice (typical role playing game dice).jpg|caption2=Various dice with different numbers of sides and distributions of values.
|image3=A_Wafer_of_the_Latest_D-Wave_Quantum_Computers_(39188583425).jpg|caption3=Dies ({{senseno|en|semiconductors}}) on a [[wafer]].
}}
{{ety|en|id=device}}
From {{inh|en|enm|dee}}, from {{der|en|fro|de}} (Modern {{cog|fr|dé}}), from {{der|en|la|datum}}, from {{m|la|datus||given}}, the past participle of {{m|la|do|dō|to give}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*deh₃-||to lay out, to spread out}}. {{doublet|en|datum}}.

Replaced {{ncog|ang|tasul}}, {{m|ang|tesul|t=die}}, from {{ncog|la|tessella|t=die, cube}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[cubical]] part of a [[pedestal]]; a [[plinth]].
# {{senseid|en|Q2609080}} A [[device]] for [[cut]]ting into a [[specify|specified]] [[shape]].
# {{senseid|en|Q1129424}} A [[device]] used to [[cut]] an [[external]] [[screw thread]]. (Internal screw threads are cut with a [[tap]].)
# A mold for forming metal or plastic objects.
# An [[emboss]]ed [[device]] used in [[stamp]]ing [[coin]]s and [[medal]]s.
# {{senseid|en|semiconductors}} {{lb|en|semiconductors|plural also [[dice]]}} An oblong chip fractured from a [[semiconductor]] [[wafer]] engineered to perform as an independent device or [[integrated circuit]].
# Any small cubical or square body.
#* {{RQ:Watts Improvement|passage=Some young creatures have learnt their letters and syllables, and the pronouncing and spelling of words, by having them pasted or written upon many little flat tablets or '''dies'''.}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|dice|s<l:nonstandard>}}

# {{senseid|en|Q45089}} An [[isohedral]] [[polyhedron]], usually a [[cube]], with [[number]]s or [[symbol]]s on each side and thrown in [[game of chance|games of chance]].
#: {{ux|en|Most '''dice''' are six-sided.}}
#: {{ux|en|I rolled the '''die''' and moved 2 spaces on the board.}}
#* {{RQ:Hume Human Understanding|Of Probability|94|If a '''Dye''' were mark’d with one Figure or Number of Spots on four Sides, and with another Figure or Number of Spots on the two remaining Sides, ’twould be more probable, that the former ſhould turn up than the latter;}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} That which is, or might be, determined, by a throw of the die; [[hazard]]; [[chance]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=II|canto=V|stanza=13|page=249|passage={{...}}For th'equall '''die''' of warre he well did know.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The game of dice is singular. Thus in "Dice is a game played with dice," the first occurrence is singular, the second occurrence is plural. See also [[dice#Usage_notes|the usage notes under "dice"]].

